. Weak memory for numbers could affect attention/accuracy.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So decision quality, stress resilience good, technical competence good, but communication and adaptability issues.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper. So reliability, attention, problem solving, responsibility good, but hot temper and know-it-all affect crew cooperation and professionalism.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate has strongest overall? Let's weigh.\n\nCandidate B: strong reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, technical (weather, computer). But nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. Could be mitigated? But hot temper also serious.\n\nCandidate C: strong decision making, calm, technical, but egocentric, communication difficulty, not willing to further education. That may be problematic for long-term development.\n\nCandidate D: strong concentration, problem solving, responsibility, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew.\n\nCandidate A: strong anticipation, spatial vision, leadership, but show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate B because strengths align with reliability and stress, and the negative (nasty remarks) is a behavior that could be addressed with training, but hot temper may be more severe? Both are serious. Need to decide.\n\nWe could start by recommending Candidate B, but we need to justify and note concerns. Or we could ask another panel member for more info on candidate B's communication style. But we have a fact: makes nasty remarks about colleagues. That's a clear concern.\n\nMaybe we should ask another panel member for more detail on Candidate D's hot temper incidents. But we need to start discussion. Could propose Candidate D as leading candidate due to strong technical and responsibility, but hot temper is concerning.\n\nGiven we need to start, we can present an initial recommendation, perhaps Candidate B, and note concerns, and ask others for input on crew cooperation aspects.\n\nThus: public message: I recommend Candidate B, because of conscientiousness, stress handling, weather assessment, but note concern about nasty remarks. I ask others for any additional observations on his crew cooperation.\n\nWe also need to include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nLet's do that."}
